<title>GERMANY: Bonn to issue about 44 bln dmk of debt in Q2.</title>
<headline>Bonn to issue about 44 bln dmk of debt in Q2.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government plans</p>
<p>to issue the following debt in the second quarter of 1997, the</p>
<p>Bundesbank as issuing agent said on Monday.</p>
<p>    PAPER	     MATURITY     VOLUME (DMK)     TIME OF ISSUE</p>
<p>Treasury discount   6 months     about 9 bln	April 16</p>
<p>paper (Bubills)</p>
<p>Federal bond	  10 years     about 15 bln     3rd 10 days</p>
<p>								  of April</p>
<p>Treasury bond	 5 years	about 10 bln     3rd 10 days</p>
<p>(Bundesobligationen)					of May</p>
<p>Treasury notes	2 years	about 10 bln     2nd 10 days</p>
<p>								  of June</p>
<p>NOTE - The planned 10-year bond will be strippable from July. The exact date of each issue will be announced one week beforehand, the Bundesbank said. The issue calendar for the third quarter of 1997 will be announced in the third 10 days of June.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
